  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Every readiness signal records what was known, when it was known, its source, and the scenario or model version that used it.",
    "Transportation cutoff uses the approved business-day calendar and recomputes when the appointment changes.",
    "Explicit symptom or transportation text bypasses model priority and routes immediately without clinical interpretation.",
    "Camila's exact immutable reply creates separate clinical-contact and transportation work with different owners, deadlines, projections, acknowledgments, and closure rules.",
    "Invalid or out-of-order commands are rejected without partial mutation, and duplicate commands or events are idempotent.",
    "SLA miss escalates, appointment change reopens affected work, and caregiver permission revocation removes future caregiver access without rewriting history.",
    "Patient, caregiver, staff, transportation, graph, timeline, and preliminary metrics derive consistently from the same committed events.",
    "Stale scheduler, source, or projection state remains visible and never appears as reassurance.",
    "Reset/reseed restores the exact finals workflow state without deleting valid Epic authorization or the last-known-good Camila snapshot.",
    "The API-backed critical journey preserves the locked visual, accessibility, responsive, and reduced-motion behavior.",
    "Confirmation requires the approved human-owned clinical disposition, current complete transport plan, and patient acknowledgment; source Epic dates are unchanged and distinguishable from the OncoReady scenario clock.",
    "Freeze readiness/engagement feature snapshots and candidate-action decision envelopes for ML and OUTREACH before their implementation; no circular dependency on the later scheduler implementation."
  ],
  "created_by": "human"
